  "abstract": "This corrected successor proves a Penrose-Schoenberg completion theorem. The selected Einstein/TEGR static constraint gives the regulated Newton self-energy as one half of a squared Green-Hilbert distance. Its pairwise matrix is conditionally negative definite, so exp(-t E_G/hbar) is a CPTP pure-dephasing semigroup whose generator is exactly the regulated Diosi-Penrose double commutator. This closes positivity and Markovian completion, while leaving the external smearing, effective Newton scale, exact MTT rate-selection identity, controlled environmental limit, and objective outcome instrument as explicit source obligations.",
